<title>USA: Fed adds permanent reserves by buying coupons.</title>
<headline>Fed adds permanent reserves by buying coupons.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve bought coupons on Wednesday, adding permanent reserves to the banking system, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts said the Fed was responding to a seasonal need for reserves in the banking system.</p>
<p>(( -- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
